---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { release, dateLabel, sourceUrl, site } from '../../lib/site';
---
<Base title="Releases" description={`Latest public stable release: ${release.latest.tag}, ${dateLabel(release.latest.date)}. Real release notes, history and validation caveats.`}>
  <div class="container"><header class="page-hero"><span class="eyebrow">Releases / Verified public publication</span><h1>What shipped.<br />And what did not.</h1><p class="lead">The latest stable release is {release.latest.tag}, published {dateLabel(release.latest.date)}. Development branches and release candidates are not silently included.</p></header>
    <div class="article-layout"><aside class="release-index" aria-label="Public release history">{release.history.map(item => <a href={`/releases/${item.tag}/`}><span>{item.tag}</span><small>{item.date}</small></a>)}<a href={`${site.repo}/releases`}>All GitHub releases <span>↗</span></a></aside><article class="prose"><div class="release-heading"><h2>{release.latest.tag}</h2><span class="badge">Latest stable</span></div><p>Context Engine, managed Claude Code and first-slice workspaces, alongside terminal and shell fixes.</p><ul><li>Demand-driven capabilities, first-party modules and declarative local Context Packs.</li><li>Status Strip 2.0, <code>/strip</code> Studio and direct <code>/modules</code> access.</li><li>Managed Claude Code targets and a keyboard-first <code>/mods</code> inventory.</li><li>Explicit worktree plans and a read-only GitHub PR/issue workspace.</li><li>Passthrough, tmux, transcript-copy and Fish input fixes.</li></ul><aside class="note"><strong>Physical-terminal QA was not performed for this release.</strong><p>Automated gates passed; hands-on testing of the new surfaces in Ghostty and Terminal.app is still pending. Linux, WSL 2 and additional hosts have open validation work. <a href="/docs/reference/physical-qa/">Open checklist →</a></p></aside><h3>Important limits</h3><p>Managed targets are Claude Code only. The GitHub workspace makes no remote changes. Context Packs install from local files, without a remote registry or executable extension tier. Fish type-ahead during <code>read</code> and a lone <code>ESC[3J</code> remain known caveats.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href={`/releases/${release.latest.tag}/`}>Full release notes <span>→</span></a><a href={release.latest.url}>GitHub release ↗</a></div><h2>One source, reviewed updates</h2><p>Version, date and release notes come from a checked-in public GitHub snapshot, verified {release.verifiedAt}. Builds work without external release data. Updating the snapshot is an explicit maintenance step, not an automatic promotion of unreleased work.</p><p><a href={sourceUrl('CHANGELOG.md')}>Canonical changelog ↗</a> · <a href="/roadmap/">Roadmap and proposals →</a></p></article></div>
  </div>
</Base>
